        {
          "id": "SP_EIRENE_HEXANEMALIS",
          "name": "Eirene hexanemalis",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Eirene",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Mature medusa 10 - 18 mm in diameter, bell hemispherical, thick apical jelly, gastric peduncle broad, length variable but usually not reaching beyond velum level. Velum narrow. Manubrium six-rayed in cross-section, perradial corners of the mouth drawn out as lips, mouth margin with many folds. Majority of individuals with six radial canals, in a minority with other numbers varying from 4 to 12. Gonads thin, more or less straight, along radial canal from base of peduncle to circular canal. 40 - 60 short tentacles on small bulbs, bulbs with adaxial, conical excretory papilla. In-between 2 tentacle bulbs 1 - 2 rudimentary bulbs (marginal warts) and 2 - 4 round statocysts with one concretion (occasionally 2 - 4, Browne, 1905 b). Polyp planktonic, solitary, see Bouillon (1983).",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:5186165"
